# Files that are generated, vendored, or intentionally full of credential-shaped
# strings. Scanning them produces noise, not findings.
#
# secretlint matches on content, so lockfiles are the main source of false
# positives: they embed base64 integrity hashes that look like high-entropy
# tokens to several rules.

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
build/
coverage/
**/coverage/
*.wasm
target/

# Lockfiles and manifests whose integrity hashes are not secrets
package-lock.json
**/package-lock.json
Cargo.lock
**/Cargo.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock

# Vendored / minified bundles
*.min.js
**/*.min.js

# Generated API and coverage reports
**/api-docs.json
**/openapi.json
**/openapi.yaml
test_snapshots/
**/test_snapshots/
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Documentation that documents placeholder credentials. These files are meant to
# be read as templates; the values are the placeholders documented next to them
# (e.g. JWT_SECRET=your-secret-key-min-8-chars), not live keys. Real keys are
# caught by the pre-commit .env check and by the rest of the scan.
**/*.env.example
.env.example
